  "notes": "West leads the ♥J against 6♠. After the defense takes the ♥A and continues the suit, South's only problem is how to play the trump suit for no losers. The correct play is to finesse East for the ♠K. That play is superior to cashing the ♠A on the first round (see hand A-3 on skill level 2).\n\nSouth must be careful how he manages the spade finesse. After crossing to the dummy in diamonds, it would be wrong to lead a low spade from dummy and finesse with the ♠J. After that start, it would be impossible to pick up the suit if East started with all 3 spades.\n\nSouth should instead begin by leading the ♠Q from the dummy intending to pass it. When East covers with the ♠K, South wins the ♠A. South crosses back to the dummy in diamonds. A finessing position now exists over East's ♠10.\n\nSouth has nothing to lose by playing spades in this way. Picking up all 3 spades in East's hand is what can be gained.",
  "commentary_paragraphs": [
    "West leads the ♥J against 6♠. After the defense takes the ♥A and continues the suit, South's only problem is how to play the trump suit for no losers. The correct play is to finesse East for the ♠K. That play is superior to cashing the ♠A on the first round (see hand A-3 on skill level 2).",
    "South must be careful how he manages the spade finesse. After crossing to the dummy in diamonds, it would be wrong to lead a low spade from dummy and finesse with the ♠J. After that start, it would be impossible to pick up the suit if East started with all 3 spades.",
    "South should instead begin by leading the ♠Q from the dummy intending to pass it. When East covers with the ♠K, South wins the ♠A. South crosses back to the dummy in diamonds. A finessing position now exists over East's ♠10.",
    "South has nothing to lose by playing spades in this way. Picking up all 3 spades in East's hand is what can be gained."
  ],
